{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>He did not remove.</b> The verb is transitive, for the Name mentioned above did not remove the pillars from before the people." "And the word יומם is not found in all of Scripture except for the time when the sun is upon the earth, for יום is found in the Torah and the Prophets and the Writings and it is night, as it is written, יום הכותי כל בכור (Numbers 5:17 — 'on the day I struck every firstborn'), and this was at night. And it is written, היום הזה יום בשורה הוא (II Kings 7:9 — 'this day is a day of good news'), and it was at night, for there it is written, ונחשוב נא עד אור הבקר (ibid. — 'let us wait until the light of morning'). And it is written, יום צעקתי בלילה נגדך (Psalms 88:2 — 'by day I cried out, in the night before You')."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:17.429233627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}